35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"I looked at the ledger and the bank statements. Seventy percent of our costs are fixed, like hall hire. We can't cut those.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I checked the sign-in sheets and the weekday turnout. A quarter of members do two-thirds of the work. And when we charged for summer outings, weekday attendance dropped by a third.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Takumi,,I compared the rota to the attendance. The same nine people set up and lock up. They are the ones who show up every single time. The others are just paying a fee to be absent.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,I reviewed the treasurer's hours and the bank statements. Chasing individual payments took six hours a month. A yearly collection took one. The current system is unsustainable.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,I read the taster forms and the mid-year joiner records. Nine people said they wouldn't commit to a whole year. And every mid-year joiner needed a hand-worked calculation. That friction is why they hesitate.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, that six hours a month is huge. If we switch to a single yearly payment, we save that time and the money is in the bank before the year starts.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, but @Takumi, if the heavy users pay the same as the ghosts, the heavy users will feel it’s unfair. They are doing the work.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, exactly. It’s not just about the money. It’s about the effort. The nine people who do everything are subsidizing the eighteen who never show up. That’s not right.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, I agree it’s unfair, but a tiered system means more calculations, more chasing, more hours for the treasurer. We can’t afford that complexity.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Toshio, I get the admin worry. But if the fee is a big lump sum, the tasters won’t come back. They need a low, simple way in.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"So we have a tension. We need the money upfront for stability, but we need to keep the door open for new people. And we need to address the fairness issue.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"The hesitation is real. When people have to weigh the cost of coming out, they don’t. We need a structure that makes belonging feel automatic, not transactional.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"I’m not asking for a punishment for the ghosts. I’m asking for a system that doesn’t reward them. If they pay the same, they are free-riding on the work of the active members.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"The only way to keep the admin load low is to have one payment. If we have tiers, we have to track who is in which tier, and that’s more hours.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"What if the base fee is low, and the active members just... do more? The fee is for belonging, not for labor. The labor is a gift.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I’m leaning towards a single, predictable fee. It covers the fixed costs, it’s easy to administer, and it’s stable. The fairness issue is real, but it’s a social problem, not a financial one.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I’m worried that a single fee, if it’s high, will create that hesitation again. But if it’s low, it might not cover the costs. We need to find the middle.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"I’m still not convinced. But I see the admin problem. If we can’t track the tiers, we can’t enforce them. So maybe the fee has to be simple, and we deal with the fairness through other means.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I’m with @Mio. The single payment is the only one that keeps the treasurer’s hours manageable. Anything else is a slow burn.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I’m with @Mio too, but only if the fee is low enough that a taster can say yes without thinking. The barrier has to be almost invisible.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
