60,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Option A is the only one that gives us the stability we need. One payment, one time, and the money is there. No chasing, no guessing.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Option C is the one that creates the hesitation. If I have to pay to come to the winter social, I have to weigh it. That’s the barrier we’re trying to remove.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"Option B is the only one that addresses the fairness. If the heavy users pay more, they are not subsidizing the ghosts. It’s the only one that feels right.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option B is a trap. It means the treasurer has to track who is in which tier, and that’s more hours. Option A is the only one that keeps the admin load low.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Option A is the one that keeps the door open. If the fee is low, a taster can say yes. Option C is the one that makes them think.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, I agree. The admin load is the killer. Option B is too complex. Option C is too fragmented. Option A is the only one that works.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, but what about the hesitation? If the fee is high, people will hesitate. We need to make sure the fee is low enough that it doesn’t create a barrier.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Mio, I’m not happy with Option A. It’s the one that rewards the ghosts. But I see the admin problem. Maybe we can deal with the fairness through other means.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, the fairness is a social problem. The admin is a financial one. We can’t solve the social problem with a financial tool. Option A is the only one that keeps the system running.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Toshio, I agree. The fee is for belonging, not for labor. The labor is a gift. Option A is the one that keeps the belonging simple.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,"I’m voting for Option A. It’s the only one that gives us the stability we need. The fairness issue is real, but it’s not a financial problem.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I’m voting for Option A, but only if the fee is low. If it’s high, it will create the hesitation we’re trying to remove.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"I’m voting for Option B. It’s the only one that addresses the fairness. I know it’s more complex, but it’s the right thing to do.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I’m voting for Option A. It’s the only one that keeps the admin load low. Anything else is a slow burn.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I’m voting for Option A. It’s the one that keeps the door open. The fee has to be low, but it has to be simple.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,I’m glad we’re on the same page. Option A is the one that works. Let’s make sure the fee is low enough that it doesn’t create a barrier.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I’m with you. The fee has to be an invitation, not a barrier. If it’s low, people will come. If it’s high, they will hesitate.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"I’m not happy, but I see the admin problem. I’ll vote for Option A, but I want us to talk about the fairness issue later.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I’m glad we’re moving forward. Option A is the only one that keeps the system running. Let’s get on with it.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
